@PRODUCT_NAME@ @VERSION@, portable build for Linux

Run it:            ./@LINUX_NAME@
Add it to the application menu for your user:   ./install-for-user.sh
Remove it from the menu:                        ./install-for-user.sh --remove

Nothing here needs administrator rights. The folder can live anywhere; run
install-for-user.sh again after moving it.

If it does not start on Ubuntu 23.10 or later

Those systems stop an ordinary program from creating the user namespace that
the built-in sandbox uses, and this folder cannot carry the root-owned helper
that is the alternative. The app then stops at start with a message about
"chrome-sandbox". Either install the .deb package instead, which sets this up,
or give the helper in this folder to root once:

  sudo chown root:root chrome-sandbox && sudo chmod 4755 chrome-sandbox

Do not start the app with --no-sandbox.

